# Airtight Alibi's flash and hexproof. Bot1's Memnite (1/1) attacks on turn 3 and is tapped on Bot2's turn 4. Bot2 casts Lightning Bolt at it; in response Bot1 flashes in the Alibi:
# the enters trigger untaps Memnite (it was not suspected, nothing else changes) and gives it hexproof, so the Bolt's only target is illegal on resolution and it
# does nothing (CR 608.2b, 702.11b). Memnite is 3/3 with no damage - without hexproof the Bolt's 3 damage would have killed it even so.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Mox Emerald
Memnite
Airtight Alibi
Island
Island
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Memnite > Bot2)
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite.Tapped = true
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Airtight Alibi.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite.Tapped = false
? Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite.Keywords = Hexproof
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite.Power = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite.Toughness = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite.Damage = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite.Tapped = false
Bot2.Graveyard.Count = 1
